            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lise Rod"
            },
            "reviewBody": "To modify this recipe the way my grandmother made these, I would use a bag of coconut to roll the raw cookies in instead of the nuts. Omit the icing. When the cookies are completely cooled, fill with assorted jams to make an array of colors for the cookie plate. Yum! We made these for Christmas season every year rather than Easter. To freeze, layer cookies with either parchment or wax paper in a sealed plastic container.",
